    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. what if the kitchen staff is spread out across different stations? like, how do we make sure the line cooks actually see these updates in real time so there isn't a mix-up during the rush? is there a specific template or checklist you'd recommend for the chef to use?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When your kitchen staff is spread out, you need a centralized, visible communication hub, like a master whiteboard or a digital display accessible to all station leads. You can't just rely on shouting instructions over the clatter of pots; the information needs to be permanently visible.\n\nI recommend a \"Critical Allergy & Dietary Needs Checklist\" template. This checklist should be printed in large, bold font and laminated, and it needs to be updated *before* service begins, not during the rush. It should list every dish, and next to it, have dedicated columns for: **\"Contains Nuts (Y/N),\"** **\"Vegan (Y/N),\"** and **\"Severe Allergy Alert (Specify).\"** This forces every cook to check off the requirements for their specific station.",
      "source": "target",
