    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the checklist sounds good. one more thing though, what if a guest asks a server about an ingredient that isn't on the label? it gets pretty chaotic when they're in line. how should the service staff handle those high-pressure questions without slowing down the whole flow or giving wrong info?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The service staff must be trained to act as a highly trained buffer, not as the final food safety authority. When a guest asks a question about an unlisted ingredient, the server should never guess or speculate, which is the most dangerous thing they can do.\n\nTheir immediate protocol should be to politely acknowledge the concern and immediately escalate it to a designated \"Dietary Liaison\"—perhaps the floor manager or the head server—who has direct, real-time access to the kitchen's master checklist. This prevents the line from stopping while ensuring the guest gets an accurate answer without the server having to risk a catastrophic mistake.",
